ential boxed warning consideration for patients >65), hepatotoxicity\n  warranting mandatory liver function monitoring, and the high discontinuation\n  rate. The Division has requested: (a) 6-month post-trial cardiac safety\n  follow-up data, (b) independent hepatic event adjudication, and (c) an\n  updated benefit-risk assessment, all prior to the Q2 2026 advisory committee\n  meeting.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n2. RIVAMOD (RVM-305) — Aethon Pharmaceuticals\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDesign: Randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled; 52 weeks; N=2,103\n         (1,052 Rivamod, 1,051 placebo); 156 centers globally\n\nEFFICACY:\n  - ACR50 at Week 24 (primary): 42% vs 18% placebo; absolute difference 24 pp\n    (95% CI: 20.1–27.9, p<0.001)\n  - DAS28-CRP remission at Week 52: 28% vs 7% placebo (p<0.001)\n  - HAQ-DI change from baseline: -0.51 vs -0.15 placebo\n\nSAFETY:\n  - Serious adverse events: 5.9% vs 5.4% placebo — near parity\n  - Treatment-related deaths: 0 in both arms\n  - MACE: 0.6% vs 0.5% placebo — no cardiovascular signal\n  - ALT elevations >3× ULN: 1.1% vs 0.9% placebo — no hepatic signal\n  - Serious infections: 1.9% vs 1.5% placebo; no opportunistic infections\n  - Most common AE: nausea 15.2% vs 4.8% (mild-to-moderate)\n  - Discontinuation due to adverse events: 6.7% vs 4.9% placebo\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3. CELVARA (CLV-220) — Meridian Biosciences\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDesign: Randomized, double-blind, active-controlled vs methotrexate; 48 weeks;\n         N=1,524 (762 Celvara, 762 methotrexate); 98 centers in NA & Europe\n\nEFFICACY:\n  - ACR50 at Week 24 (primary): 39% vs 32% methotrexate; absolute difference\n    7 pp (95% CI: 2.3–11.7, p=0.018)\n  - DAS28-CRP remission at Week 48: 24% vs 19% methotrexate (p=0